The Federal Republic of Germany
The results of the Census are broken down by region according to the existing hierarchy of administrative levels. This is based on the regional code, which is uniformly assigned by the statistical offices of the Federation and the Länder and has the following structure: 
1st and 2nd digit = Land code; 
3rd digit = administrative region code; 
4th and 5th digit = rural or urban district code; 
6th to 9th digit = association code; 
10th to 12th digit = municipality code. 
The leading digit of the four-digit association code indicates the type of municipality: 
0 = municipality not belonging to an association of municipalities; 
5 = municipality belonging to an association of municipalities; 
9 = area not attached to a municipality. 
The areas not attached to a municipality are not relevant for the Census.

In terms of administrative levels, the "administrative region" level is only available for the following Länder: Baden-Württemberg, Bayern, Hessen, Niedersachsen (here: "statistical region"), Nordrhein-Westfalen and Sachsen.

The "association of municipalities" level is only available for the following Länder: Brandenburg, Mecklenburg-Vorpommern, Niedersachsen, Rheinland-Pfalz, Sachsen, Sachsen-Anhalt, Schleswig-Holstein and Thüringen.

